Starting today, the Apple TV streaming service is offering a new selection of "bonus" movies in the U.S., Canada, the U.K., and some other countries.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/04/New-Apple-TV-Logo.jpeg" alt="" width="1600" height="901" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1043659" /><br/>
While competitors like Netflix offer an extensive catalog of movies from various studios, Apple TV primarily offers its own original films produced by Apple. Over the past few years, however, Apple has offered a "Great Movies Now on Apple TV" section with a limited rotation of iconic movies that subscribers can watch at no additional cost.<br/>
<br/>
